$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (method E1) A mixture of boronic acid (5.0 mmol), tert-butyl
(2-bromoallyl)(methyl)carbamate (0.9 eq), XPhos (0.06 eq), potassium
triphosphate monohydrate (2.0 eq), ethanol (10 mL) and H2O (5 mL) in a
dry microwave vial was degassed using nitrogen gas for 10 mins. In case
of 75, SPhos (0.06 eq) and nbutanol were used. Palladium (II) acetate
catalyst (2 mol%) was subsequently added. In case of 82 and 85, boron
pinacol ester 80 (1 eq), aryl bromide (1.5 eq), XPhos (0.1 eq), potassium
triphosphate monohydrate (3.0 eq), and palladium (II) acetate catalyst (5
mol%) were used. The mixture was further degassed for 5 mins and then
sealed with a cap. The reaction was heated at 60 °C for 16 h. When the
reaction was completed, the solvents were removed in vacuo and the
residue was partitioned between EtOAc and H2O. The organic layer was
washed twice with H2O, dried over MgSO4, filtered and concentrated. The
crude product was purified by column chromatography. The pure products.
tert-Butyl ethyl(2-phenylallyl)carbamate (75) Following method E1, the
title compound was isolated as an oil (92%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ
7.44 – 7.39 (br. s, 2H), 7.34 – 7.27 (m, 3H), 5.40 (br. d, 1H), 5.12 (s,
1H), 4.28 (br. d, 2H), 3.20 (br. d, 2H), 1.45 (s, 9H), 1.06 (br. s, 3H).
13C NMR (100 MHz, Chloroform-d) δ 155.6/155.2, 144.6, 139.6/138.9, 128.2,
127.7, 126.3, 113.5/113.0, 79.4, 50.0/49.3, 40.7, 28.4.
