$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure A -Sequential Suzuki-Hiyama Reaction i. To a 5 mL round
bottomed flask equipped with a magnetic stirrer bar and reflux condenser
is added MIDA-vinyl silane 1, Pd(OAc)2 (5 mol%) SPhos (10 mol%) and aryl
halide (1.2 equiv.) and the mixture purged with argon for 5 min after
which dioxane (0.08M) was added and the solution stirred for a further 10
min. K3PO4 solution (7.5 equiv., 3M solution degassed) was then added and
the mixture stirred at 60 °C until TLC analysis showed complete
consumption of starting material (TLC eluted with EtOAc). The mixture was
diluted with DCM and passed through a pad of Celite, washing with DCM and
EtOAc and the solution concentrated. The residue was redissolved in dry
THF (1M), followed by the addition of the requisite aryl iodide (1.5 eq).
The mixture was purged under argon, followed by the addition of TBAF (2
equiv, 1M in THF) and the resulting mixture stirred at 25 °C for 30 min.
Pd2dba3.CHCl3 (2.5 mol%) was then added and the dark brown solution
stirred at 25 °C for 6 hours. The mixture was diluted with DCM, passed
through a pad of Celite washing with DCM and concentrated/ The residue
was purified by flash column chromatography to afford the requisite
product. (E)-1-methyl-4-styrylbenzene (4b). The title compound was
prepared according to general procedure A, using vinylborane 2 (38 mg,
0.12 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (1.3 mg, 5.7 μmol), SPhos (4.7 mg, 11.4 μmol),
iodobenzene (28 mg, 0.14 mmol) and K3PO4 (0.28 mL, 0.86 mmol) in dioxane
(1.4 mL) and stirred at 60 °C overnight. After filtration through Celite,
concentration and redissolving the residue in THF (0.1 mL), 4-iodotoluene
(37 mg, 0.17 mmol) and TBAF (0.23 mL, 0.23 mmol) were added followed by
the addition of Pd2dba3.CHCl3 (3.0 mg, 2.9 μmol) and the mixture stirred
for 6 hours. Filtration through Celite and flash column chromatography.
4b (21 mg, 92%) as a colourless solid. Rf (Hexane) = 0.41; 1H NMR: (400
MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.50 (2H, d, J = 7.3 Hz), 7.41 (2H, d, J = 8.0 Hz), 7.34
(3H, t, J = 7.3 Hz), 7.27-7.21 (1H, m), 7.16 (2H, d, J = 8.0 Hz), 7.1
(1H, d, J = 16.3 Hz), 7.04 (1H, d, J = 16.3 Hz), 2.36 (3H, s); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 137.5, 137.5, 134.5, 129.4, 128.6, 128.6, 127.7,
127.4, 126.4, 126.4, 21.2. All spectra are in accordance to those
previously reported.2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Hiyama cross-coupling reaction (stages 3-4), Suzuki
coupling (stages 1-2)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM MIDA-Vinylsilanes: Selective Cross-Couplings and Applications to the
Synthesis of Functionalized Stilbenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM McLaughlin, Mark G.; McAdam, Catherine A.; Cook, Matthew J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2015), 17(1), 10-13

